+// PATCHED (HOA Connect). Upstream resolves a request literal against the union
+// of every generated API route, scoring each candidate with per-segment
+// template-literal recursion. At ~229 routes that runs at TypeScript's
+// instantiation-depth limit: whichever `$fetch` call the checker reaches first
+// fails with TS2321 "Excessive stack depth", and the failure MOVES to the next
+// call site if you rewrite the one that reported it. It is marginal rather than
+// broken — an unrelated file changing size is enough to tip it either way.
+//
+// Exact match only. Static routes keep their handler's response type, which is
+// all but a handful of the app's ~233 call sites; routes carrying `:params` or
+// a `**` catch-all fall back to the default response type and need an explicit
+// annotation at the call site. Nothing relied on that inference when this
+// landed (typecheck: 0). Types only — no runtime behaviour changes.
+//
+// Re-check this on every nitropack upgrade; pnpm refuses to apply the patch if
+// the version moves, so it cannot go stale silently.
+type MatchedRoutes<Route extends string> = Route extends keyof InternalApi ? Route : never;
 
